{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011UcQFNEmQ1Qz43DicG8J2R","type":"tool_result","content":"      \"id\": \"US-162\",\n      \"title\": \"Add React 19.2 cacheSignal() for Server Component fetch cleanup\",\n      \"priority\": \"low\",\n      \"description\": \"React 19.2 introduces cacheSignal() for Server Components, providing an AbortSignal that fires when the cache() entry's lifetime ends. This allows in-flight fetch requests to be aborted when the cached result will no longer be used (e.g., when cache is invalidated mid-request). For server-side data fetching (room availability, pricing from external APIs), cacheSignal ensures abandoned fetches don't hold open connections unnecessarily.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"At least one cache() function wrapping an external fetch uses cacheSignal() to pass an abort signal\",\n        \"Fetch requests are aborted when the cache entry is invalidated (verified via network tab — no hung requests)\",\n        \"No TypeScript errors when using cacheSignal() (requires React 19.2 types from Next.js 16)\",\n        \"Server Component rendering is not regressed (same data fetched correctly)\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"cacheSignal() is Server Components only — not usable in Client Components or Route Handlers\",\n        \"Pattern: const dedupedFetch = cache((url) => fetch(url, { signal: cacheSignal() }))\",\n        \"React 19.2 feature, available with Next.js 16\",\n        \"Source: https://react.dev/reference/react/cache#caching-with-a-signal\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"model\": \"haiku\",\n      \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-14T01:52:04Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-163\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Google Tag Manager with Consent Mode v2\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"description\": \"Install GTM with Consent Mode v2 so all six consent parameters (ad_storage, ad_user_data, analytics_storage, ad_personalization, functionality_storage, personalization_storage) are correctly signalled before any Google tags fire. Required since March 2024 for Google Ads conversion tracking to function with EU/international visitors. Enables the marketing team to manage tags without code deploys.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"GTM container script loaded in layout.tsx using @next/third-parties/google GoogleTagManager component\",\n        \"Consent Mode v2 default state is set to 'denied' before GTM loads via a gtag.js dataLayer push in a beforeInteractive script\",\n        \"All six consent parameters are initialised: ad_storage, ad_user_data, analytics_storage, ad_personalization, functionality_storage, security_storage\",\n[rerun: b2]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b67213d-2eef-4ac1-bb69-724ff9b6a3c0","uuid":"e628e622-fb9f-411b-b52b-be88e1d77e9b","timestamp":"2026-04-14T01:53:17.124Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"      \"id\": \"US-162\",\n      \"title\": \"Add React 19.2 cacheSignal() for Server Component fetch cleanup\",\n      \"priority\": \"low\",\n      \"description\": \"React 19.2 introduces cacheSignal() for Server Components, providing an AbortSignal that fires when the cache() entry's lifetime ends. This allows in-flight fetch requests to be aborted when the cached result will no longer be used (e.g., when cache is invalidated mid-request). For server-side data fetching (room availability, pricing from external APIs), cacheSignal ensures abandoned fetches don't hold open connections unnecessarily.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"At least one cache() function wrapping an external fetch uses cacheSignal() to pass an abort signal\",\n        \"Fetch requests are aborted when the cache entry is invalidated (verified via network tab — no hung requests)\",\n        \"No TypeScript errors when using cacheSignal() (requires React 19.2 types from Next.js 16)\",\n        \"Server Component rendering is not regressed (same data fetched correctly)\"\n      ],\n      \"technicalNotes\": [\n        \"cacheSignal() is Server Components only — not usable in Client Components or Route Handlers\",\n        \"Pattern: const dedupedFetch = cache((url) => fetch(url, { signal: cacheSignal() }))\",\n        \"React 19.2 feature, available with Next.js 16\",\n        \"Source: https://react.dev/reference/react/cache#caching-with-a-signal\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimatedComplexity\": \"small\",\n      \"passes\": false,\n      \"model\": \"haiku\",\n      \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-14T01:52:04Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-163\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Google Tag Manager with Consent Mode v2\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"description\": \"Install GTM with Consent Mode v2 so all six consent parameters (ad_storage, ad_user_data, analytics_storage, ad_personalization, functionality_storage, personalization_storage) are correctly signalled before any Google tags fire. Required since March 2024 for Google Ads conversion tracking to function with EU/international visitors. Enables the marketing team to manage tags without code deploys.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"GTM container script loaded in layout.tsx using @next/third-parties/google GoogleTagManager component\",\n        \"Consent Mode v2 default state is set to 'denied' before GTM loads via a gtag.js dataLayer push in a beforeInteractive script\",\n        \"All six consent parameters are initialised: ad_storage, ad_user_data, analytics_storage, ad_personalization, functionality_storage, security_storage\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014gT8w86D4yTG46er8n8pr5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! I found story US-162. Let me review the requirements:\n\n**Story US-162:** \"Add React 19.2 cacheSignal() for Server Component fetch cleanup\"\n\n**Description:** React 19.2 introduces cacheSignal() for Server Components, providing an AbortSignal that fires when the cache() entry's lifetime ends. This allows in-flight fetch requests to be aborted when the cached result will no longer be used (e.g., when cache is invalidated mid-request). For server-side data fetching (room availability, pricing from external APIs), cacheSignal ensures abandoned fetches don't hold open connections unnecessarily.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n1. At least one cache() function wrapping an external fetch uses cacheSignal() to pass an abort signal\n2. Fetch requests are aborted when the cache entry is invalidated (verified via network tab — no hung requests)\n3. No TypeScript errors when using cacheSignal() (requires React 19.2 types from Next.js 16)\n4. Server Component rendering is not regressed (same data fetched correctly)\n\n**Technical Notes:**\n- cacheSignal() is Server Components only — not usable in Client Components or Route Handlers\n- Pattern: const dedupedFetch = cache((url) => fetch(url, { signal: cacheSignal() }))\n- React 19.2 feature, available with Next.js 16\n- Source: https://react.dev/reference/react/cache#caching-with-a-signal\n\n**Dependencies:** None\n\n**Complexity:** small\n\n**Current status:** passes: false, last_attempted: 2026-04-14T01:52:04Z\n\nNow let me read the progress.txt to understand the codebase context.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":73205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893},"output_tokens":