{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01FL3KV5uQH5Yx9fqvkmJtrW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! The project is using:\n- React 19.2.0 ✓\n- Next.js 16.1.6 ✓\n\nBoth support cacheSignal(). Now let me create my plan:\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n**Files to create:**\n1. `site/src/lib/cache-utils.ts` - Utility function for cacheSignal() pattern\n\n**Files to modify:**\n1. `site/src/components/Rooms.tsx` - Add a demonstration of cacheSignal() usage\n\n**Approach:**\n- Create a cache utility that wraps a fetch with cacheSignal()\n- Update the Rooms component to demonstrate the cacheSignal() pattern with a simple external API call\n- Ensure no TypeScript errors\n- Keep it simple and focused\n\nLet me start by creating the diagnosis block and plan as required by the Ralph protocol.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1636,"cache_read_input_tokens":85797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1636},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b67213d-2eef-4ac1-bb69-724ff9b6a3c0","uuid":"15141909-3437-468b-9440-a5599a8634b9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01FL3KV5uQH5Yx9fqvkmJtrW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Current State\n\nThe Pelangi Capsule Hostel website uses Next.js 16.1.6 and React 19.2.0 (both support cacheSignal()). The Rooms.tsx component is already a Server Component using `\"use cache\"`, `cacheLife()`, and `cacheTag()`. However, there's no usage of the `cache()` function wrapped with `cacheSignal()` for external fetches yet.\n\n## Problem Identified\n\nStory US-162 requires implementing React 19.2's `cacheSignal()` API which provides an AbortSignal that fires when a cache entry's lifetime ends. This allows automatic abort of in-flight fetch requests when the cache is invalidated. Currently, no external fetches use this pattern.\n\n## Planned Changes\n\n- Create `site/src/lib/cache-utils.ts` with a utility function demonstrating the cacheSignal() pattern\n- Update `site/src/components/Rooms.tsx` to demonstrate cacheSignal() with an example external data fetch\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [\"site/src/lib/cache-utils.ts\"],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\"site/src/components/Rooms.tsx\"],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [\"getCachedExternalData\"],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 45\n}\n</plan>\n\nNow let me implement this. First, I'll create the cache utility:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1636,"cache_read_input_tokens":85797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1636},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b67213d-2eef-4ac1-bb69-724ff9b6a3c0","uuid":"6595611d-1629-42f2-8783-317af2bd364d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01FL3KV5uQH5Yx9fqvkmJtrW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018YVPCQvZ95yg67MqGBmBRQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\lib\\cache-utils.ts","content":"import { cache } from \"react\";\nimport { cacheSignal } from \"react\";\n\n/**\n * Creates a cached fetch function that aborts in-flight requests when\n * the cache entry's lifetime ends. This uses React 19.2's cacheSignal()\n * to receive an AbortSignal that fires when cache invalidation occurs.\n *\n * Usage:\n * const data = await getCachedData(url);\n */\nexport const getCachedData = cache(async (url: string) => {\n  const signal = cacheSignal();\n  const response = await fetch(url, { signal });\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error(`Failed to fetch from ${url}: ${response.status}`);\n  }\n  return response.json();\n});\n\n/**\n * Example: Fetch room availability from an external API with cacheSignal.\n * When the cache entry expires, the fetch is automatically aborted,\n * preventing hung connections and unnecessary resource usage.\n */\nexport const getCachedRoomAvailability = cache(async (roomId: string) => {\n  const signal = cacheSignal();\n  const apiUrl = `https://api.example.com/availability/${roomId}`;\n\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(apiUrl, {\n      signal, // AbortSignal that fires when cache lifetime ends\n      headers: {\n        \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n      },\n    });\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      throw new Error(`API returned ${response.status}`);\n    }\n\n    return await response.json();\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error instanceof Error && error.name === \"AbortError\") {\n      // Cache was invalidated mid-request — abort signal fired\n      console.log(`Fetch for room ${roomId} was aborted by cache invalidation`);\n      throw error;\n    }\n    throw error;\n  }\n});\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1636,"cache_read_input_tokens":85797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1636},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b67213d-2eef-4ac1-bb69-724ff9b6a3c0","uuid":"2b4e9517-6955-4f42-90fd-fab8ecc495ff"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018YVPCQvZ95yg67MqGBmBRQ","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\lib\\cache-utils.ts"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b67213d-2eef-4ac1-bb69-724ff9b6a3c0","uuid":"669189ce-e010-4a4e-a731-3b5da692e287","timestamp":"2026-04-14T01:54:36.384Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\lib\\cache-utils.ts","content":"import { cache } from \"react\";\nimport { cacheSignal } from \"react\";\n\n/**\n * Creates a cached fetch function that aborts in-flight requests when\n * the cache entry's lifetime ends. This uses React 19.2's cacheSignal()\n * to receive an AbortSignal that fires when cache invalidation occurs.\n *\n * Usage:\n * const data = await getCachedData(url);\n */\nexport const getCachedData = cache(async (url: string) => {\n  const signal = cacheSignal();\n  const response = await fetch(url, { signal });\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error(`Failed to fetch from ${url}: ${response.status}`);\n  }\n  return response.json();\n});\n\n/**\n * Example: Fetch room availability from an external API with cacheSignal.\n * When the cache entry expires, the fetch is automatically aborted,\n * preventing hung connections and unnecessary resource usage.\n */\nexport const getCachedRoomAvailability = cache(async (roomId: string) => {\n  const signal = cacheSignal();\n  const apiUrl = `https://api.example.com/availability/${roomId}`;\n\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(apiUrl, {\n      signal, // AbortSignal that fires when cache lifetime ends\n      headers: {\n        \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n      },\n    });\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      throw new Error(`API returned ${response.status}`);\n    }\n\n    return await response.json();\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error instanceof Error && error.name === \"AbortError\") {\n      // Cache was invalidated mid-request — abort signal fired\n      console.log(`Fetch for room ${roomId} was aborted by cache invalidation`);\n      throw error;\n    }\n    throw error;\n  }\n});\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_013smLonHzkh3mjas1xBeYkm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've created the cache utility. Now I need to update the Rooms.tsx component to use the new cacheSignal() pattern. I'll demonstrate the pattern being used by making a commented-out example that shows how to use it, and also add an actual working example if it makes sense.\n\nLet me think about what to add to the Rooms component. I can:\n1. Add a call to getCachedData() to fetch some external data (like weather or exchange rates)\n2. Or just add a comment showing how it would be used\n\nSince the acceptance criteria require \"at least one cache() function wrapping an external fetch uses cacheSignal()\", I should actually call the function. Let me fetch something useful like exchange rates or weather for JB as an example.\n\nActually, looking at the component, I don't want to change its core functionality too much. I could add a data fetch that returns some useful information (like nearby attractions or exchange rates) that could be displayed.\n\nLet me add a simple function that fetches exchange rates or some public API data, and integrate it into the component in a way that doesn't break the existing functionality.\n\nActually, a better approach would be to create a separate component that demonstrates the cacheSignal() pattern, and then include it in the Rooms component. Or I can just modify the Rooms component to call the cached fetch function.\n\nLet me keep it simple: I'll add a simple function call that fetches some data using cacheSignal(), and store it in a variable. This demonstrates that the pattern is being used.\n\nActually, looking at it more carefully - I need to make sure the fetch actually happens. Let me add a simple data fetch to the Rooms component that uses the cacheSignal pattern. I'll fetch some public data (like a \"did you know\" fact) from a simple API or just create mock data.\n\nWait, I should think about this more carefully. The acceptance criteria say:\n1. \"At least one cache() function wrapping an external fetch uses cacheSignal()\"\n2. \"Fetch requests are aborted when the cache entry is invalidated (verified via network tab — no hung requests)\"\n\n\n3. \"No TypeScript errors when using cacheSignal()\"\n4. \"Server Component rendering is not regressed\"\n\nSo I need to create a cache() function with cacheSignal() in the utility, use it in a Server Component, ensure no TypeScript errors, and verify the component still renders properly. The simplest approach is to import getCachedData into Rooms and call it with a public API endpoint, storing the result to demonstrate the pattern works without disrupting existing functionality.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1161,"cache_read_input_tokens":87433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1161},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b67213d-2eef-4ac1-bb69-724ff9b6a3c0","uuid":"5d0174b3-dd1a-4c35-b65c-d57a67c7f2ae"}
