{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01H6zamLpGi2KVqfFJJM3TCg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D3Vuoy6svReDwM8uSa2ba9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd 'C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website' && rtk git add prd.json site/src/lib/cache-utils.ts site/src/components/Rooms.tsx && rtk git commit -m \"feat(US-162): Add React 19.2 cacheSignal() for Server Component fetch cleanup\n\nImplemented React 19.2's cacheSignal() API for automatic fetch abort when cache entries are invalidated.\n\nChanges:\n- Created lib/cache-utils.ts with getCachedData() utility using cache() and cacheSignal()\n- Added getCachedRoomAvailability() example for room availability fetches from external APIs\n- Updated Rooms.tsx Server Component to demonstrate cacheSignal() pattern\n- Gracefully handle AbortError when cache invalidation occurs\n\nThe cacheSignal() AbortSignal ensures that in-flight fetch requests are automatically terminated when the cache entry's lifetime ends, preventing hung connections and unnecessary resource usage.\n\nStory ID: US-162\nAcceptance criteria met:\n- [x] At least one cache() function wrapping an external fetch uses cacheSignal()\n- [x] Fetch requests aborted when cache entry is invalidated (handled via AbortError)\n- [x] No TypeScript errors when using cacheSignal() (build successful)\n- [x] Server Component rendering is not regressed (all 83 pages generated)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\"","description":"Commit implementation of US-162"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":619,"cache_read_input_tokens":103176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":619},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool